{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Mr Brennan, sorry now, we're after running a bit late. Come on through. I took your blood pressure while you were waiting, 146 over 82, and the pulse was 74.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Ah you're grand. I wasn't minding the wait. Desperate rain, I was half drowned off the bus.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (DOCTOR): Sit yourself down there, Pat. You're very welcome. How've you been keeping?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Not too bad, doctor. I was nearly going to stay home, only the neighbour told me I was a fool to ignore a rash.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (DOCTOR): Neighbours have plenty of opinions. What's actually bothering you today?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Well. It's a burning, on the one side of me chest. And there's a few blisters come up.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (DOCTOR): Right. Tell me a bit more about that burning. Which side, and what does it feel like?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): The left side. It's a burning sort of a pain, sore enough. I don't know, doctor, it's hard to put words on it.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (DOCTOR): How long has that been going on?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm. Two days. Yeah, two days now.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (DOCTOR): Did the blisters come up at the same time?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): They did, yeah, the same two days. A few of them on the same side. I spotted them getting dressed.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any fever with this, or have you felt shivery at all?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): No. I'm not hot. I don't think I've had a shiver.",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any cough, or a tightness when you breathe?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No cough. Breathing is grand.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (DOCTOR): Grand. Would you open the shirt a second and let me see?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. It's along here, under the arm and across a bit. Sorry, the shirt's damp from the rain.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (DOCTOR): I can see a small cluster of blisters on the left side of the chest. They stop at the midline, they don't cross over.",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (DOCTOR): Did you ever have the chickenpox, when you were a child?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): I did, yeah. Ages ago. I don't know, doctor, I couldn't tell you when. Not last winter or the one before, I was small, I haven't a clue of the year.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (DOCTOR): Lots of people can't date it, that's fine. The chickenpox virus can sit quiet in a nerve for years and then come back out like this. It looks like shingles to me.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): Shingles. Ah god. Is that desperate?",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (DOCTOR): It can be very sore, but we've caught it early. I'm going to start you today on an antiviral, aciclovir, 800 milligrams, five times a day, for seven days.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): Five times a day. I already take the water tablet in the morning, for the blood pressure. They won't fight with each other, will they? I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (DOCTOR): They won't. You keep on with the water tablet every morning, and you add the aciclovir through the day.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't know the dose of the water tablet at all. The chemist just hands me the box. I'm on it since last winter, or maybe the winter before. I couldn't say.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (DOCTOR): That's alright, it'll be on your file. Now, is there anyone calling to the house who's pregnant?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): My daughter. She's expecting, the summer. She's in and out the whole time.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (DOCTOR): Until the blisters crust over, I'd keep her at a bit of distance. No minding you up close, and no hugging. The rash can pass the chickenpox virus on, and that's a worry in pregnancy.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): She was over yesterday evening. I don't know, doctor, is that awful?",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (DOCTOR): Yesterday is yesterday. From today, cover the rash with a clean cloth, wash your hands, and give her a ring to say keep back for the next while.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): Right. And the burning, will that settle?",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (DOCTOR): It should ease once the aciclovir gets going. If the pain is still fierce after the seven days, come back in to me and we'll see about the nerve pain.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): Am I alright to walk down to the chemist myself? For that, umm, asyclovir. I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (DOCTOR): You are, as long as the rash is covered. I'll write the aciclovir now so you can take the first dose today.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (PATIENT): Grand so. Umm. Do I stop the water tablet? No, you said keep it. Sorry.",
  "[SEG0038] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): I'll have the prescription at the desk for you, Mr Brennan, so you're not hanging about.",
  "[SEG0039] person_3 (DOCTOR): Good man. Mind yourself, and make that call to your daughter this evening."
 ],
